# [Ticket #43 superseded this rule — removed 2026-09-18] trailingSlash is now
# "always" (astro.config.mjs), and i18n/utils.ts localizedPath() always emits
# a trailing slash, matching BaseLayout's canonical tag, hreflang alternates,
# JSON-LD, every internal <a href>, and the sitemap. The rule that used to
# live here (`/*/  /:splat  301`) stripped the trailing slash on every
# request — i.e. it 301-redirected every page's own canonical URL to a
# DIFFERENT URL than the one it declares itself to be. That is a live
# redirect/canonical-mismatch bug: the canonical URL never returns 200 with
# its own content, so Google can neither trust nor index it. No replacement
# rule is needed — Cloudflare Pages' static asset handler already serves
# dir/index.html for both /path and /path/ with a 200, and by default
# auto-redirects the non-slash form to the slash form, which now agrees with
# every signal above (the same zero-hand-written-rule mechanism
# pickmytrade.trade already relies on).

